    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d743">

                <pb facs="0815" n="803" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg803"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.00/1810: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Diplomatic Agent and Consul General at Tangier</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">White</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-12-24T11:00:00+01:00">December 24,
                            1940—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>93. My telegram to the Department 89, December 18, 4 p.m. My British colleague is
                    proceeding to Madrid today to help draft a project of a <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >modus vivendi</hi> with the Spanish Government for British interests in
                    Tangier.</p>
                <p>The Legation’s telegram No. 92, December 21, 9 p.m.,<anchor n="35"
                        xml:id="d743-f1"/> please disregard the final paragraph.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">White</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
